   - <v(g)> x <uniq_Opnd>: Interaction of cyclomatic complexity with unique operands, highlighting dependencies between code logic and operand diversity.

2. Density measures:
   - <v(g)> / <loc> (Cyclomatic complexity per line of code): Determines defect density relative to code complexity.
   - <e> / <loc> (Effort per line of code): Quantifies development effort scaled by code size.
   - <iv(g)> / <loc> (Design complexity density): Shows design complexity normalized by code size.

3. Proportions:
   - <ev(g)> / <v(g)> (Essential complexity ratio): Shows the proportion of essential complexity to the cyclomatic complexity, which indicates structured logic.
   - <branchCount> / <v(g)> (Branch-to-complexity ratio): Evaluates the branching density relative to cyclomatic complexity.

4. Volume vs. effort ratios:
   - <v> / <e> (Volume-to-effort ratio): Captures the efficiency of representing the logical volume of code given the effort.
   - <v> / <locCodeAndComment> (Volume efficiency ratio): Relates logical program volume to the lines of code plus comments.

### Nonlinear Transformations:
5. Logarithmic transformations on some skewed features to handle scale variance and distribute values more evenly:
   - <log> <v> (Log volume).
   - <log> <e> (Log effort).
