6. Scaling and normalization:
   - <i> x <d> (Scaled intelligence): Scaling Halstead intelligence by difficulty captures the effective cognitive requirements of the code.
   - <log_effort> / <loc> (Effort density per log-transformed effort): Normalizes logarithmic effort to code size for sensitivity analysis.

### Combinations to explore:
- <effort_per_loc> x <v_g_per_loc>: Combines effort per line and cyclomatic complexity per line to analyze aggregated density patterns.
- <scaled_intelligence> x <v>: Interaction between scaled Halstead intelligence and volume measures code understandability in relation to size.
